// ConnectHS — example build configuration.
//
// SETUP (one-time, after fresh checkout):
//   cp ConnectHS/Config.example.xcconfig ConnectHS/Config.xcconfig
//   Then edit Config.xcconfig with your real Supabase project values.
//
// Config.xcconfig is gitignored — your real credentials never leave your
// machine. This template is what gets committed.
//
// Find the values in your Supabase dashboard:
//   - SUPABASE_URL host: Project Settings → API → Project URL (everything
//     after https:// — for example "abcdefgh.supabase.co"). The https://
//     prefix is added in code so the host stands alone here.
//   - SUPABASE_ANON_KEY: Project Settings → API → "anon public" key. This
//     ships in the iOS binary; RLS protects data, so it's safe.
//
// xcconfig syntax: `//` starts a comment, so URLs inside values must
// escape it. We avoid that here by storing only the host (no scheme) and
// prepending https:// in SupabaseClient.swift.

SUPABASE_URL = YOUR_PROJECT_REF.supabase.co
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY = YOUR_ANON_PUBLISHABLE_KEY
